Makes DuckDuckGo the default search engine where Chrome's is Google, which ungoogled-chromium
makes an engine that searches nowhere. As the fallback it's the default and not the user's choice,
so a recommended DefaultSearchProvider policy outranks it until the user picks an engine, as it
outranks Google in Chrome. A locale with no country, such as C or POSIX, has no DuckDuckGo in its
list, so the fallback brings its own.

--- a/components/search_engines/template_url_prepopulate_data.cc
+++ b/components/search_engines/template_url_prepopulate_data.cc
@@ -317,9 +317,14 @@
     PrefService& prefs,
     const std::vector<raw_ptr<const PrepopulatedEngine>>&
         regional_prepopulated_engines) {
-  return FindPrepopulatedEngineInternal(prefs, regional_prepopulated_engines,
-                                        google.id,
-                                        /*use_first_as_fallback=*/true);
+  // browser_core: DuckDuckGo in Google's place, from the list if it's in it.
+  if (std::unique_ptr<TemplateURLData> engine =
+          FindPrepopulatedEngineInternal(prefs, regional_prepopulated_engines,
+                                         duckduckgo.id,
+                                         /*use_first_as_fallback=*/false)) {
+    return engine;
+  }
+  return TemplateURLDataFromPrepopulatedEngine(duckduckgo);
 }

 }  // namespace TemplateURLPrepopulateData
